 twisting on the 2-Selmer group\u003C/em\u003E, Math. Proc. Cambridge Philos. Soc. \u003Cstrong\u003E145\u003C/strong\u003E (2008), no. 3, 513\u0026ndash;526. \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2464773\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E2464773\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004108001588\u0022\u003E10.1017/S0305004108001588\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E C. Videla, \u003Cem\u003ESobre el d\u0026eacute;cimo problema de Hilbert\u003C/em\u003E, Atas da Xa Escola de Algebra, Vitoria, ES, Brasil. Colecao Atas 16 Sociedade Brasileira de Matematica, 1989, pp. 95\u0026ndash;108.\n\u003Cli\u003E Ju. G. Zarhin, \u003Cem\u003ENoncommutative cohomology and Mumford groups\u003C/em\u003E, Mat. Zametki \u003Cstrong\u003E15\u003C/strong\u003E (1974), 415\u0026ndash;419 (Russian). \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=354612\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E354612\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E \u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E D. Zywina, \u003Cem\u003ERank one elliptic curves and rank stability\u003C/em\u003E, Preprint, arXiv:\u003Ca href=\u0022https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.16960\u0022\u003E2505.16960\u003C/a\u003E.\n\u003C/ul\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E","BibliographicInfo":"\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EPeter Koymans\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EAffiliation: Mathematisch Instituut, Universiteit Utrecht, Postbus 80.010, 3508 TA Utrecht, The Netherlands\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMR Author ID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?mrauthid=1208557\u0027\u003E1208557\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EORCID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7582-4149\u0027\u003E0000-0002-7582-4149\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EEmail: p.h.koymans@uu.nl\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ECarlo Pagano\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EAffiliation: Department of Mathematics and Statistics, Montreal, Quebec H3G 1M8, Canada\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMR Author ID: \u003Ca href=\u0027https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?mrauthid=1233159\u0027\u003E1233159\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EEmail: carlein90@gmail.com\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EReceived by editor(s): December 11, 2024\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EReceived by editor(s) in revised form: January 29, 2025, April 22, 2025, October 6, 2025, October 29, 2025, November 24, 2025, March 28, 2026, and April 27, 2026\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EPublished electronically: August 10, 2026\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EAdditional Notes: The first author was supported by the Dutch Research Council (NWO) through the Veni grant \u201CNew methods in arithmetic statistics\u201D.\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u0026copy; Copyright 2026\nAmerican Mathematical Society\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EJournal: J. Amer. Math. Soc.\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EMSC (2020): Primary 11G05, 03D35, 03D25, 11D99\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EDOI: https://doi.org/10.1090/jams/1081\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E","PdfUrl":"/0000-000-00/S0894-0347-2026-01081-8/S0894-0347-2026-01081-8.pdf","HtmlUrl":null,"Authors":[{"RelationshipType":"AUTHOR","FullName":"Peter Koymans","FirstName":"Peter","MiddleName":" ","LastName":"Koymans","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":"KYPTXB","MRAuthorId":1208557,"Email":"p.h.koymans@uu.nl","CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":"Mathematisch Instituut, Universiteit Utrecht, Postbus 80.010, 3508 TA Utrecht, The Netherlands","AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null},{"RelationshipType":"AUTHOR","FullName":"Carlo Pagano","FirstName":"Carlo","MiddleName":" ","LastName":"Pagano","Suffix":" ","MasterCustomerId":"PGCRXE","MRAuthorId":1233159,"Email":"carlein90@gmail.com","CustomerSequence":0,"Affiliation":"Department of Mathematics and Statistics, Montreal, Quebec H3G 1M8, Canada","AffiliationSequence":0,"FirstEditor":false,"Url":null,"Description":null,"BookReviewId":0,"CurrentAddress":null}],"BookReviews":[],"AMSCopyrightFlag":"Y","CopyrightOwner":"American Mathematical Society","MRNumber":null,"ArticleCitation":"J. Amer. Math. Soc.","CrossReferences":"","Abstracts":[],"IsAMSCopyright":true,"PostDateFormatted":"August 10, 2026"},{"ArticleId":92845,"JournalProductCode":"JAMS","IssueId":null,"ManuscriptId":1080,"DocumentType":"ARTICLE","Title":"The correlation energy of the electron gas in the mean-field regime","DOI":"10.1090/jams/1080","PII":"S0894-0347-2026-01080-6","Issue":null,"IssueDirectory":"0000-000-00","StartPage":null,"EndPage":null,"PostDate":"2026-07-31T00:00:00","PrimaryMsc":"81V74","SecondaryMsc":null,"MscSchema":"2020","Abstract":"We prove a rigorous lower bound on the correlation energy of interacting fermions in the mean-field regime for a wide class of singular interactions, including the Coulomb potential. Combined with the upper bound obtained by Christiansen, Hainzl, and Nam [Comm. Math. Phys. 401 (2023), pp. 1469\u20131529], our result establishes an analogue of the Gell-Mann\u2013Brueckner formula $c_{1}\\rho \\log \\left (\\rho \\right )\u002Bc_{2}\\rho$ for the correlation energy of the electron gas in the high-density limit. Moreover, our analysis allows us to go beyond mean-field scaling while still covering the same class of potentials.","EnhancedReferences":"\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Bach%2C%20Volker\u0022\u003EVolker Bach\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EError bound for the Hartree-Fock energy of atoms and molecules\u003C/em\u003E, Comm. Math. Phys. \u003Cstrong\u003E147\u003C/strong\u003E (1992), no.\u0026nbsp;3, 527\u0026ndash;548.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1175492\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E1175492\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02097241\u0022\u003E10.1007/BF02097241\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Boccato%2C%20Chiara\u0022\u003EChiara Boccato\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Brennecke%2C%20Christian\u0022\u003EChristian Brennecke\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Cenatiempo%2C%20Serena\u0022\u003ESerena Cenatiempo\u003C/a\u003E, and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Schlein%2C%20Benjamin\u0022\u003EBenjamin Schlein\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem\u003EBogoliubov theory in the Gross-Pitaevskii limit\u003C/em\u003E, Acta Math. \u003Cstrong\u003E222\u003C/strong\u003E (2019), no.\u0026nbsp;2, 219\u0026ndash;335.  \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=3974476\u0022\u003EMR \u003Cstrong\u003E3974476\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/a\u003E, DOI \u003Ca href=\u0022https://doi.org/10.4310/ACTA.2019.v222.n2.a1\u0022\u003E10.4310/ACTA.2019.v222.n2.a1\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\n\n\n\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Benedikter%2C%20Niels\u0022\u003ENiels Benedikter\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Nam%2C%20Phan%20Thanh\u0022\u003EPhan Th\u0026agrave;nh Nam\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Porta%2C%20Marcello\u0022\u003EMarcello Porta\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Schlein%2C%20Benjamin\u0022\u003EBenjamin Schlein\u003C/a\u003E, and \u003Ca href=\u0022https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/search/authors.html?authorName=Seiringer%2C%20Robert\u0022\u003ERobert Seiringer\u003C/a\u003E, \u003Cem